# The sample plan sheet is WRITTEN BY A TEST, not by hand.
#
# `test/planSheetSample.test.js` regenerates docs/sample-plan-sheet.html, and the
# generated bytes were platform-dependent: the sheet embeds app.css and is built
# from template literals in sources that git checks out as CRLF on Windows, so
# the output carried CRLF while the committed file was LF. Every `npm test` left
# the tree dirty with a file whose content was identical once endings are
# normalised -- `git diff` showed nothing, `git status` showed a modification.
#
# That is worse than untidy: a permanently dirty tree trains people to ignore
# `git status`, and this estate depends on reading it before staging (CLAUDE.md
# says so explicitly). Both sessions hit it independently.
#
# The test now normalises to LF when it writes, which is the actual fix. This
# line keeps the checkout matching, so the two cannot disagree again.
docs/sample-plan-sheet.html text eol=lf
